E2e4.Chess.Fics.Client is released under the MIT licence, see LICENSE. It has no dependency on GPL code: timeseal is
supplied by the application through ITimesealCodec (see README.md).

The files in tests/E2e4.Chess.Fics.Client.Test/Fixtures are synthetic. They keep the shape of FICS protocol traffic
(style-12 board lines, game-end lines, [G] timeseal pings, login prompts), which is how the protocol works, and nothing
else from a real session: the banner, message of the day, help text, other players' handles and contact details were
replaced, and the guest handles are made up. They are released under the same MIT licence.

"FICS" and "freechess.org" are used only to say which server this library talks to. This project is not affiliated with
FICS or its administrators.
